course: dictionary
lesson: 4108
title: A bird's gizzard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name one special thing, and you can find their meaning from the clues around them. «Birds have no teeth; a muscly part of the stomach called the gizzard grinds their food, often with swallowed grit.» Birds have no teeth, so something else must grind the food. The sentence says it is a muscly part of the stomach, so a gizzard must be a strong, squeezing part of the stomach.
explain: Look at the clue «swallowed grit». Grit means tiny bits of stone or sand. The bird swallows these on purpose, and they help crush the food. Try your meaning in the sentence: «a strong muscly part of the stomach grinds the food» still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Gizzard also has an informal, funny meaning. People sometimes say «It sticks in my gizzard» when something annoys them. Nobody has a real gizzard stuck in their body here. The words are a figure of speech, so the meaning is about feelings, not about a body part.
fact: A gizzard is a strong, muscular part of a bird's stomach.
fact: The gizzard grinds up food, which is its main job.
fact: Birds have no teeth, so swallowed stones and grit help the gizzard crush food.
fact: «Ostriches swallow pebbles, which collect in the gizzard and grind tough food.»
fact: Informal: «It sticks in my gizzard» means it annoys me.
exercise: «Birds have no teeth; a muscly part of the stomach called the gizzard grinds their food.» What is a gizzard? | A small stone found in a river | A type of bird's beak | *A strong, muscly part of a bird's stomach that grinds food | A pocket for keeping seeds
exercise: «Ostriches swallow pebbles, which collect in the gizzard.» Why do birds swallow pebbles? | To stop them from flying | To keep their feet warm | To make their feathers shine | *To help grind tough food in the gizzard
exercise: Mia says, «It sticks in my gizzard.» What does the phrase really mean? | I have swallowed a stone | I am very hungry | *It annoys me | I like the taste of it
test: What does the gizzard do in a bird? | It keeps the bird warm | *It grinds food, often with swallowed stones | It helps the bird fly faster | It makes the bird sing
test: Which word means a strong, muscly part of a bird's stomach? | Feather | Wing | *Gizzard | Beak
exam: Why do birds without teeth swallow little stones? | *So the stones help grind tough food in the gizzard | So they can see in the dark | So they can float on water | So they can talk to other birds
